UnitRelayInitialize
├── when initializing twice
│   └── it should revert with AlreadyInitialized
├── when an operator input is zero
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the compounder is zero
│   └── it should skip the grant instead of reverting
├── when both entrypoints are zero
│   ├── it should revert on a maxi relay which can never attach one
│   ├── it should revert on a protocol relay starting as level one
│   └── it should initialize a protocol relay starting as level two which attaches later
├── when the config is degenerate
│   └── it should reject zero windows zero floors and a zero entrypoint timelock
├── when a seed invariant is broken
│   └── it should reject a foreign, empty or lock-mismatched seed
├── when the module is not authorized
│   └── it should revert with ModuleNotAuthorized
├── when a maxi starts as level two
│   └── it should revert with NotPromotable
├── when a constructor dependency is zero
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when a satellite implementation holds no code
│   ├── it should revert with ImplementationNotAContract for the principal implementation
│   ├── it should revert with ImplementationNotAContract for the yield implementation
│   └── it should hold the zero address to the same rule, since it carries no code either
├── when a satellite clone comes out unwired
│   ├── it should revert with SatelliteNotInitialized when the clone never bound the relay
│   └── it should revert with SatelliteNotInitialized when the clone dropped the transferability
├── when granting the standing compound allowance
│   └── it should approve the escrow for the maximum amount and the module for the stake
├── when naming the reward token at initialization
│   ├── it should register the named token
│   ├── it should close the single slot registry on it, leaving the keeper nothing to add
│   └── it should leave the registry empty when the creator names no token
├── when extending a custom period lock
│   └── it should refresh only when the end falls short of the horizon
├── when the lock already covers the horizon
│   └── it should never reach the escrow
├── when extending a permanent lock
│   └── it should never reach the escrow
├── when allocating with a custom period lock
│   ├── it should refresh the staking period before the dispatch
│   └── it should emit the allocation
├── when compounding after a custom period lock fell short
│   └── it should refresh the staking period before growing the stake
├── when compounding while the lock still holds the horizon
│   └── it should skip the refresh
├── when the lock weeks reach past the escrow maximum
│   └── it should revert with LockWeeksTooLong
├── when the lock weeks sit at the escrow maximum
│   └── it should accept the config
├── when initializing the satellite implementations
│   └── it should revert with AlreadyInitialized on both implementations
└── when copying the config into the clone
    └── it should copy every field verbatim
